From b83973dd83b86075cf7060e01d2b3d2c18a7d79d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LGNative <luis@nativestride.io>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 18:14:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/28] TR Importer: EUR conversion fix + manual-cash-transfer
 mapping
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The v3.5 core converts a holding's quote currency to its base currency via FX
when they differ — it only needs the FX:<ccy>/EUR rate to exist. New
tr-fx-pairs.ts reads the actual quote currency of each held asset and creates
the missing FX pairs (source YAHOO, seeded live from the ECB) via the SDK, then
syncs + recalculates. Wired to a 'Fix EUR conversion' button in the EUR view.
This is what un-inflated the portfolio (USD shown as EUR → real EUR).

Also map TR's MANUAL_CASH_TRANSFER (e.g. a goodwill/compensation payment) by
amount sign → DEPOSIT / WITHDRAWAL, so it's no longer skipped as Unknown Type.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
